  "coverage_boundary": "The first-order residue annihilates the entire S-linear correction module, and the annihilator is proved exactly by two polynomial identities and the period. The quadratic result uses every possible relevant homogeneous component; its finite matrices are exhaustive by weights. Ordinary nonlifting, two-fold quantum ramification, finite copies, identity spectators, actual canonical transport and regular spatial formal corrections use the written proofs. For arbitrary quantum ramification a persistent reducing block is an additional hypothesis; no automatic block lifting or all-ramified exclusion is asserted. The ordinary rank-one forward Long graph has zero compressed Poisson defect and is not excluded. No actual Long carrier or DC2/JC2 solution is claimed.",
